Figure 4 demonstrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are actively transported to the draining lymph nodes by antigen-presenting cells (APCs). The percentage of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells in the lymph nodes peaks at Day 2 post-injection at 3.5% (Panel B). Migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) consistently represent the largest proportion (60–80%) of Nano-11-positive cells across different time points (Panel C) and exhibit the highest mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) per cell (Panel D), indicating their prominent role in internalizing and transporting Nano-11.